phases.prompt:
Plan where to look, given what has been settled.

System: {state:scope.system}
Symptom: {state:scope.symptom}
An answer looks like: {state:scope.answered_when}
Not yet known: {state:scope.unknowns}

Name the sources worth consulting, most likely to be decisive first. A source is somewhere an answer could actually come from: a log, a config file, a metric, the output of a command, a document, a person.

Then say what shape the work takes. Use "parallel" when the sources can be checked independently and none depends on another's result. Use "sequential" when one result decides what to look at next. Use "mixed" when some can go together and the rest must wait on them.

List the first moves concretely enough to act on. Three or four, not ten: a plan that names every possible check is a plan nobody follows, and it hides which check actually mattered.

Do not carry out the work here.
